	(text "EoS KL25 Board, rev A. Designed by Kartikeydheer Srivastava. Fits Uno R3 shields; 3.3 V I/O.\nCopyright (c) 2026 Kartikeydheer Srivastava. All rights reserved; see LICENSE.txt.\nValues from NXP KL25P80M48SF0 (data sheet), KL25P80M48SF0RM, KLQRUG, AN3208, AN1706;\nSilicon Labs CP2102N Rev. 1.5, TI SLVSFG1A (TPS2116), Diodes DS37274 (AP7361C), ST LIS2HH12.\nFirmware: run the 8 MHz oscillator in low-power mode (MCG_C2[HGO] = 0): high-gain mode\nwould overdrive the crystal (AN3208 Eqn. 1), and RF must not be fitted (DS Table 19)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 260 360 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f151256c-065c-5a3b-be9e-b53a5ac97016")
	)
	(text "Power: J1 (KL25 USB) or J2 (UART USB), each through its PTC fuse to the TPS2116,\nwhich takes J1 whenever it is present and blocks reverse current. The CP2102N runs\nfrom 3.3 V and senses J2's VBUS (R15, R16); R27 bleeds mux leakage off VBUS2, so it\nconnects only when a host is on J2."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 400 330 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4e8baffc-7198-5698-8289-50b651dd4933")
	)
